/* Synastry house overlays: what it means when a partner's planet falls in one of your houses. */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.synastry = window.AstroDeep.synastry || {};

window.AstroDeep.synastry.overlays = {
  sun: {
    1: "Their Sun lights up your 1st house, so around them you feel seen, often in a way that is flattering and a little exposing at once. They notice how you present yourself and tend to encourage you to take up more space. You may find yourself standing taller, dressing with more confidence or trying on new ways of being. The risk is shaping your identity around their approval, so keep checking that the version of you they bring out is one you actually like.",
    2: "With their Sun in your 2nd house, this person has a strong effect on what you value and how you handle money. They may boost your confidence in your own worth, or bring practical opportunities that improve your income. You might start to see your talents as real assets for the first time. There can also be friction if they hold firm views on how you spend or save. Learn from their outlook, and keep your financial choices your own.",
    3: "Their Sun falls in your 3rd house, which puts conversation at the heart of this connection. Talking with them feels lively and easy, and you may find yourself texting, swapping links and chatting about everything from errands to big ideas. They tend to sharpen your thinking and make you curious about new subjects. Occasionally their opinions can drown yours out in everyday exchanges, so make sure the dialogue stays two-way and your own voice keeps its place.",
    4: "When their Sun lands in your 4th house, this person feels like home, or stirs up strong feelings about home and family. You may want to live with them, cook for them or introduce them to relatives early on. They can warm your private life and help you feel rooted. They may also remind you of a parent, for better or worse. Notice when old family patterns replay between you, and choose which ones are worth keeping.",
    5: "Their Sun in your 5th house brings play, flirtation and creative spark. Time with them can feel like a holiday: you laugh more, take small risks and rediscover what you actually enjoy. This is a classic romantic overlay, and it can also light up a creative or parenting partnership. The shadow is that the fun can stay on the surface if neither of you moves toward commitment. Enjoy the delight, and be honest about whether you want more.",
    6: "With their Sun in your 6th house, this person shows up in the practical fabric of your days. They may shape your routines, your work habits or your health, nudging you to exercise, eat better or get organised. You often work well together on tasks. Over time the bond can feel more like a useful arrangement than a thrilling romance, and you might feel quietly managed. Appreciate their steadiness while keeping room for spontaneity and rest.",
    7: "Their Sun in your 7th house is one of the strongest partnership indicators. You tend to see them as a natural partner, someone who fits the shape of what you look for in a significant other, and commitment can feel like an obvious next step. Because this house also holds projection, you may see qualities in them that you have not yet claimed in yourself. Let them inspire you, rather than asking them to carry what you could develop on your own.",
    8: "When their Sun falls in your 8th house, the connection goes deep quickly. You may feel exposed, intrigued and intensely drawn to them, with strong sexual chemistry and a sense that they see straight through your defences. Shared money, debts or resources can also become a theme. This overlay can transform you by bringing buried feelings to the surface. It can also stir jealousy or power struggles, so keep honesty and consent at the centre of everything.",
    9: "Their Sun in your 9th house widens your world. They may introduce you to new cultures, philosophies or places, and you often learn a great deal simply by being around them. You might travel together, study together or argue happily about the meaning of life late into the night. You tend to look up to them as a teacher or guide. Just watch for putting them on a pedestal, because even inspiring people have ordinary flaws.",
    10: "With their Sun in your 10th house, this person affects your ambitions and public image. They may champion your career, open doors or push you to aim higher than you would on your own. Being seen together can matter to you, and their presence can raise your standing. At times they may feel like an authority figure whose expectations weigh on you. Take the encouragement, and keep defining success by your own measure.",
    11: "Their Sun lands in your 11th house, which gives the bond a friendly, easy quality. Whatever else you are to each other, you tend to be good friends first. They may bring you into new social circles or encourage your hopes for the future, and planning together feels natural. If this is a romance, the challenge is keeping it personal rather than merely companionable, so make time for closeness as well as shared causes and group outings.",
    12: "When their Sun falls in your 12th house, the connection feels mysterious and hard to name. You may sense that they understand parts of you nobody else sees, or feel slightly undone around them without knowing why. There can be a spiritual or fated flavour, and sometimes secrecy. This overlay can be deeply healing when it brings hidden feelings into the light. It can also blur your boundaries, so stay clear about what is actually happening between you."
  },
  moon: {
    1: "Their Moon in your 1st house means they respond to you instinctively. They pick up on your moods, react strongly to how you look and carry yourself, and can make you feel emotionally noticed from the first meeting. A protective feeling often runs both ways. Because their feelings are so tuned to you, you might also start to feel responsible for their emotional weather. Enjoy the warmth, and remind yourself that their moods are not always about you.",
    2: "With their Moon in your 2nd house, they feel emotionally tied to your sense of security. They may want to look after you in practical ways: feeding you, helping with money or making sure you have what you need. You can feel more grounded and valued around them. Money and possessions may also carry emotional weight between you, so talk openly about spending and saving before small differences quietly turn into hurt feelings.",
    3: "Their Moon falls in your 3rd house, so everyday conversation is full of feeling. You chat easily about the small stuff of daily life, and they often respond emotionally to your ideas, which can leave you feeling truly heard. Even small talk becomes intimate. The risk is that offhand comments land harder than you meant, because they take your words personally. Speak with care, and invite them to say what they feel rather than guessing.",
    4: "When their Moon lands in your 4th house, you have one of the most homely overlays there is. You feel comfortable with them in private, as though they belong in your kitchen or at your family table, and living together often feels natural. Childhood feelings can surface too, and they may stir memories of how you were cared for. That can heal, or it can repeat old patterns. Stay aware of which one is happening.",
    5: "Their Moon in your 5th house brings emotional warmth to pleasure and play. They enjoy your creativity, respond to your affection and may bring out a childlike delight in you. Romance has a tender, nurturing quality, and this can be lovely for raising children or sharing creative projects. Their moods can swing your fun up or down, though. Keep some pleasures that belong only to you, so your joy does not depend on how they feel that day.",
    6: "With their Moon in your 6th house, they tend to care for you through daily routines. They might notice when you are tired, remind you to eat or quietly take on chores. Working side by side often feels comfortable. You may also find their moods seeping into your work and wellbeing, especially if you share a home or an office. Build routines that support you both, and speak up if caretaking starts to feel like fussing.",
    7: "Their Moon in your 7th house often signals deep emotional compatibility in partnership. You tend to feel that they need you and you need them, and a committed bond can form without much effort. They respond to you as a partner in the fullest sense, with care and loyalty. Because feelings run through the relationship itself, dependency can creep in. Keep your own friendships and inner life strong, so the partnership stays a choice rather than a lifeline.",
    8: "When their Moon falls in your 8th house, emotional intensity is close to guaranteed. You may feel they reach into your deepest fears and desires, and intimacy can be powerful and raw. There is a sense of shared vulnerability, and joint finances can become emotionally loaded. This overlay can be profoundly bonding. It can also stir possessiveness or insecurity on either side. Name your fears plainly, because hidden feelings grow stronger in this house.",
    9: "Their Moon in your 9th house draws out your curiosity about life's bigger questions. They feel at home in your beliefs and may share your longing to explore, whether that means travel, study or spiritual practice. You can feel emotionally supported in growing beyond where you started. Differences in faith or worldview can hit them personally, though. Hold your views lightly in conversation, and treat those differences as something to explore together.",
    10: "With their Moon in your 10th house, they are emotionally invested in your public life and ambitions. They may glow with pride at your achievements, or fret about your reputation and choices. Sometimes this looks like mothering your career, with steady support or strong opinions about your next move. You might feel nurtured in your goals, or watched. Let them in on your plans, and keep the final say over your direction.",
    11: "Their Moon lands in your 11th house, so you tend to feel like friends with a real emotional bond. They care about your hopes, fit comfortably into your social world and may feel like family among your friends. Planning the future together comes naturally. If you are partners, the connection can sometimes feel more affectionate than passionate. Nurture the friendship, and add deliberate moments of romance so tenderness does not settle into routine.",
    12: "When their Moon falls in your 12th house, they sense feelings you keep hidden, sometimes before you notice them yourself. You may feel soothed in a quiet, almost spiritual way, or oddly unsettled without knowing why. There can be a sense of old familiarity, or of caring for each other in ways no one else sees. This overlay can soften old wounds. It can also breed confusion if things stay unsaid, so gently put your inner world into words."
  },
  mercury: {
    1: "Their Mercury in your 1st house means they notice you and say so. They comment on your appearance, your manner and your choices, often with sharp and accurate observation. You may feel mentally switched on just by being near them, and they can help you describe yourself more clearly than before. At times their remarks can feel like critique. Take what is useful, and tell them which kinds of feedback help and which ones sting.",
    2: "With their Mercury in your 2nd house, conversations often turn to money, resources and what really matters to you. They might offer practical financial ideas, help you price your work or talk you through a budget. This can sharpen your thinking about value and self-worth in useful ways. They may also question your spending habits more than you like. Listen for the practical wisdom, and keep decisions about your own money firmly in your hands.",
    3: "Their Mercury falls in your 3rd house, a very talkative overlay. You tend to think on the same wavelength, finish each other's sentences and never run out of things to say. Messages fly back and forth all day, and you learn from each other constantly. The main danger is that talking replaces feeling, or that you both start debating for sport. Enjoy the easy flow, and now and then slow down to say what matters most.",
    4: "When their Mercury lands in your 4th house, they talk with you about home, family and your past. They may ask about your childhood, help you plan domestic life or bring an intellectual liveliness into your private space. You might work from home together or discuss family matters more openly than usual. Sometimes their curiosity can feel intrusive. Share at your own pace, and let your home be a place for quiet as well as conversation.",
    5: "Their Mercury in your 5th house makes flirting feel like a game of wit. They enjoy your humour, your creativity and your playful side, and conversation crackles with banter and ideas. They can encourage your creative projects or help you find words for what you want to express. Romance may sometimes stay in the head, with words carrying more heat than action. Delight in the wordplay, and let it lead somewhere real.",
    6: "With their Mercury in your 6th house, they have plenty to say about your daily habits, health and work. This can be genuinely useful: they may help you organise, solve nagging problems or plan better routines, and you often work well together on practical tasks. It can also slip into nagging or nitpicking. Welcome their input where it helps, and set clear limits on how much of your routine is open for discussion.",
    7: "Their Mercury in your 7th house puts communication at the centre of your partnership. You tend to talk things through as equals, negotiate well and genuinely value each other's opinions. Agreements, plans and shared decisions come fairly easily. They may also be quick to point out where the relationship needs adjusting, which can feel like a running commentary. Keep conversations fair and balanced, and remember that listening well matters as much as a clever reply.",
    8: "When their Mercury falls in your 8th house, conversations go deep. They may ask probing questions, raise taboo subjects or help you understand your own psychology better. You might share secrets early. They could also advise on shared money, debts or inheritances. This overlay can be illuminating, but their curiosity can start to feel like an investigation. Share what you choose to share, and ask them to be equally open in return.",
    9: "Their Mercury in your 9th house makes them a mental guide or a travelling companion. They broaden your thinking with new books, ideas and viewpoints, and conversations easily turn philosophical. You may plan trips, study together or debate belief over long dinners. They can challenge your assumptions in genuinely useful ways. Just watch for lecturing on either side, and treat differences of opinion as an adventure rather than a contest.",
    10: "With their Mercury in your 10th house, they think a lot about your career and public image. They may offer strategic advice, introduce you to useful contacts or help you put your goals into words. You might even work together professionally. Their opinions on your ambitions can carry real weight, sometimes more than they should. Take the useful counsel, and keep your own vision of your path clear and spoken aloud.",
    11: "Their Mercury lands in your 11th house, so talking about the future, friends and shared causes comes naturally. They may introduce you to people, connect you with groups or help you brainstorm big plans. The friendship feels mentally alive, and you inspire each other's goals. If romance is involved, it may lean toward the cerebral. Balance the ideas with warmth, touch and time spent simply being together without an agenda.",
    12: "When their Mercury falls in your 12th house, communication has a subtle, sometimes confusing quality. They may sense what you are thinking without being told, or say things that reach you on a level you cannot quite explain. You might share private conversations nobody else hears. Misunderstandings arise easily, especially when things go unspoken. Write things down when it matters, and use the bond to explore dreams, intuition and inner life."
  },
  venus: {
    1: "Their Venus in your 1st house means they find you attractive, and they tend to show it. You may feel admired, beautiful and at ease in your own skin around them, and this overlay often sparks instant chemistry. Compliments come easily and feel sincere. It can also tempt you to lean on their approval for how you look and who you are. Enjoy being appreciated, and let their affection support your self-love rather than replace it.",
    2: "With their Venus in your 2nd house, they appreciate your values, possessions and talents, and may be generous with gifts or practical help. Sharing pleasures, good food and comfort comes easily, and you may feel more secure and valued around them. There can also be a tendency to indulge together or to tangle love up with money. Enjoy the comfort, and keep an honest eye on shared spending and who pays for what.",
    3: "Their Venus falls in your 3rd house, so talking together feels sweet and easy. They like the way you think and speak, and conversations are affectionate and light. You may swap love notes, favourite songs and small daily pleasures. This overlay softens disagreements, though it can also make hard conversations harder, because neither of you wants to spoil the mood. Say the difficult things kindly, but do say them.",
    4: "When their Venus lands in your 4th house, they bring beauty and affection into your home life. They may love your space, help you decorate it or make it feel cosier simply by being there, and family members often warm to them. You can feel deeply comfortable and loved in private. Just make sure the peace at home is real, not kept up by avoiding friction. A home can hold honesty as well as ease.",
    5: "Their Venus in your 5th house is a classic sign of romance and attraction. You tend to have fun together, flirt easily and enjoy dates, art and pleasure side by side. They admire your creativity and bring out your playful heart, and it can genuinely feel like falling in love. The question over time is whether romance can deepen into commitment. Let the joy last, and build the steadier parts of the relationship too.",
    6: "With their Venus in your 6th house, affection shows up in everyday care. They may help with chores, make your routines more pleasant or look after your health in small thoughtful ways. Working together is often harmonious. This is a gentle, practical kind of love. It can occasionally feel less romantic than you want, or the service can become one-sided. Appreciate the daily kindness, and make space for celebration and treats too.",
    7: "Their Venus in your 7th house is one of the classic marriage overlays. You tend to see them as a loving, harmonious partner, and they often want commitment with you. Cooperation comes easily, and the relationship can feel balanced and graceful. Because it feels so good, you may both avoid conflict. Lasting partnership also needs honest disagreement, and you still need your own identity inside it, so keep both alive.",
    8: "When their Venus falls in your 8th house, attraction is deep and magnetic. Sexual chemistry can be strong, and love may feel transformative, even fated. They may also share money or resources generously with you. This overlay can bring real intimacy and a sense of being wanted all the way through. It can also stir possessiveness or jealousy. Let the closeness reveal you, and watch for any urge to control or be controlled.",
    9: "Their Venus in your 9th house brings a love of adventure and shared learning. They may admire your beliefs, share your taste in travel and culture, and enjoy exploring the world with you. Relationships across distance or cultures are common with this overlay, and you can grow a great deal together through experience. Keep the romance grounded in ordinary daily life too, not only in trips, big ideas and plans for somewhere else.",
    10: "With their Venus in your 10th house, they appreciate your ambitions and public image. They may admire your achievements, support your career or lift your reputation simply by being at your side. You might work well together in creative or social fields, and being seen as a couple can matter to you both. Make sure the love is about who you are, not only what you have achieved or how you look to others.",
    11: "Their Venus lands in your 11th house, so friendship and affection blend easily. They enjoy your friends, share your hopes and may help you build the future you want. You tend to feel supported, liked and at ease. This overlay can start as friendship and turn into love, or remain a warm platonic bond. If you want romance, say so, because the comfortable friendly tone can make it hard to shift gears.",
    12: "When their Venus falls in your 12th house, love has a secret, dreamy or sacrificial quality. You may feel a quiet, spiritual tenderness toward them, or the relationship may stay hidden from others for a while. They can be a healing presence in your inner life. There can also be confusion, idealisation or unspoken longing. Bring the connection into the light gently, and check that what you feel matches what is real."
  },
  mars: {
    1: "Their Mars in your 1st house energises you, sometimes more than you asked for. They push you to act, compete and assert yourself, and physical attraction can be immediate. You may feel bolder and more confident around them, or more irritated and defensive. Arguments can flare fast and burn out just as quickly. This overlay works best when you treat the energy as fuel for shared activity, whether sport, projects or passion, rather than for conflict.",
    2: "With their Mars in your 2nd house, they stir up your relationship with money and security. They may push you to earn more, spend boldly or stand up for your values. That can motivate you to build real resources and ask for what you are worth. It can also cause tension over finances, possessions or what counts as worthwhile. Agree on who handles what, and keep big spending decisions away from heated moments.",
    3: "Their Mars falls in your 3rd house, so conversations are energetic and sometimes combative. They challenge your ideas, debate you and get you thinking faster than usual. Everyday exchanges carry a charge, and you may genuinely enjoy the sparring. Sharp words can wound, though, especially when either of you is tired or stressed. Keep debates about ideas rather than character, and agree on a signal for when a discussion is turning into a fight.",
    4: "When their Mars lands in your 4th house, they bring energy, and sometimes disruption, into your home. They may help renovate, push for a move or shake up long-standing family dynamics. You can feel motivated to change your private life for the better. Tension at home is also possible, as they may trigger old family conflicts or unsettle your sense of safety. Make sure home stays a place where you can rest, not only a place of action.",
    5: "Their Mars in your 5th house brings passion, playfulness and competitive fun. Physical chemistry tends to be strong, and they may urge you to take creative or romantic risks you would normally avoid. Sport, games and adventurous dates suit this overlay well. It can also bring impulsive drama and a taste for testing each other. Keep the excitement healthy by channelling it into shared adventures and honest desire rather than jealousy games.",
    6: "With their Mars in your 6th house, they energise your daily routines and work. They may motivate you to exercise, get organised or finally tackle tasks you have been avoiding, and working together can be very productive. It can also feel like pressure, criticism or a constant argument over who does what. Divide responsibilities clearly, and notice whether their pace actually suits your body and health or slowly wears you down.",
    7: "Their Mars in your 7th house brings strong attraction and a fair share of friction. They challenge you as a partner, and you may feel drawn to them and provoked by them in equal measure. This can create a vital, honest relationship where conflict leads to growth and nothing festers. It can also turn adversarial. Learn to argue well: clear, direct and fair, with the aim of solving the problem rather than winning.",
    8: "When their Mars falls in your 8th house, sexual intensity and emotional power run high. The attraction can be consuming and genuinely transformative. They may also stir issues around shared money, control or trust, and old fears can surface quickly. This overlay can bring breakthrough intimacy, or bruising power struggles. Stay honest about your desires and your limits, and be wary of either of you using sex or money as leverage.",
    9: "Their Mars in your 9th house fires up your appetite for adventure and learning. They may push you to travel, enrol in a course or take a public stand for what you believe. Discussions about religion, politics or philosophy can get heated, and fast. At its best this overlay is excellent for shared quests and bold journeys. Keep debates respectful, because each of you can feel strongly about being right and neither likes to back down.",
    10: "With their Mars in your 10th house, they push your ambitions forward. They may drive you to compete, chase promotions or take bold career risks, and working together can generate serious momentum. There can also be clashes over authority, or a feeling that they are steering your public path more than you want. Welcome the motivation and the kick of competition, and keep the actual career decisions firmly in your own hands.",
    11: "Their Mars lands in your 11th house, so they energise your friendships and plans for the future. They may push you to join groups, launch projects or fight for causes you care about, and together you can get a remarkable amount done. Conflict can arise within shared social circles or over clashing visions of where you are heading. Keep your goals aligned, and do not let group dynamics pull the two of you into rivalry.",
    12: "When their Mars falls in your 12th house, their energy works on you in hidden ways. You may feel stirred up without knowing why, or catch yourself swallowing anger around them. There can be secret attraction or unspoken tension humming under the surface. This overlay can bring buried issues up for healing, but only if they are named. Raise frustrations early and gently, so they do not harden into resentment or passive aggression."
  },
  jupiter: {
    1: "Their Jupiter in your 1st house makes you feel bigger, luckier and more confident. They believe in you, encourage you and bring out your generous, optimistic side, and you may feel you could take on almost anything with them nearby. People often notice you looking happier. The only real risk is excess: too much indulgence, too many promises. Enjoy the lift, and let their faith in you become faith you keep in yourself.",
    2: "With their Jupiter in your 2nd house, they can be genuinely good for your finances and self-worth. They may bring opportunities, generous help or simply a more hopeful attitude to money, and you might feel more abundant and valued with them. There is a risk of overspending together or leaning on their generosity. Use the expansion wisely by building resources that last, rather than just enjoying a lucky run.",
    3: "Their Jupiter falls in your 3rd house, so talking with them opens your mind. They encourage your ideas, introduce you to new learning and make everyday life feel more hopeful. You may study together, take short trips or start writing again. This overlay is warm and encouraging, and your confidence in your own thinking tends to grow. Occasionally they overpromise or exaggerate. Take their enthusiasm as inspiration, and check the details before acting.",
    4: "When their Jupiter lands in your 4th house, they bring warmth, generosity and growth into your home life. They may help you find a bigger home, soften family tension or simply make your private world more joyful. You tend to feel secure and supported with them. There can be a tendency to overdo hospitality or spend too much on the house. Enjoy the abundance, and keep your home life grounded and liveable.",
    5: "Their Jupiter in your 5th house is a joyful overlay. They bring fun, generosity and good humour to romance, creativity and play, and you may feel luckier in love and freer to express yourself. It can also be a lovely connection for having children or sharing creative work. Watch for overindulgence or reckless risk-taking in the name of pleasure, and keep the joy balanced with some genuine commitment.",
    6: "With their Jupiter in your 6th house, they improve your daily life. They may support your health, point you toward better job opportunities or simply make work more enjoyable. You tend to feel backed up in your routines, and chores feel lighter when they are around. This overlay can also bring excess, like too many commitments or too much rich food. Take the help and optimism, and keep your routines sustainable.",
    7: "Their Jupiter in your 7th house brings generosity and good fortune to partnership. You may see them as a wise, supportive partner who helps you grow into a bigger version of yourself, and commitment feels expansive rather than restricting. Occasionally expectations run too high, and you may idealise what the relationship will deliver. Keep your hopes realistic, and let the partnership grow at its own natural pace.",
    8: "When their Jupiter falls in your 8th house, shared resources and intimacy expand. They may bring financial benefit, deep trust or a calming influence on your fears. Intimacy can feel generous, relaxed and liberating, and you may find it easier to be vulnerable. There is some risk of relying too much on their resources, or of taking emotional or financial gambles together. Enjoy the openness, and keep money agreements clear.",
    9: "Their Jupiter in your 9th house is a wonderful overlay for growth. They expand your horizons through travel, study, philosophy or faith, and you may feel you learn more with them than you ever did alone. Shared adventures come naturally, and you tend to bring out each other's optimism. The risk is treating them as a guru, or always chasing the next horizon. Let the growth also show in how you live day to day.",
    10: "With their Jupiter in your 10th house, they are good for your career and reputation. They may open doors, offer mentoring or simply believe in your ambitions so fully that you start believing too. You can feel lucky and well supported in public life. Occasionally this breeds overconfidence or overcommitting. Accept the backing gladly, and do the steady, unglamorous work that turns opportunity into lasting success.",
    11: "Their Jupiter lands in your 11th house, so friendships and future plans expand. They may introduce you to generous, interesting people, help your goals grow bigger and encourage a wider social life. You feel optimistic about what the two of you can build together. The main risk is spreading yourselves thin across too many plans and too many people. Choose a few shared dreams that really matter, and see them through.",
    12: "When their Jupiter falls in your 12th house, they bring healing and protection to your inner life. You may feel quietly supported, spiritually uplifted or forgiven in their presence, often without anything being said. This overlay can help you release old fears and regrets. There can also be vagueness or unrealistic hopes about where things are going. Enjoy the peace they bring, and keep enough clarity to see the relationship as it is."
  },
  saturn: {
    1: "Their Saturn in your 1st house can feel serious from the very start. They may be critical of how you present yourself, or you may simply feel judged and self-conscious around them. At the same time, they often help you mature, take yourself seriously and build confidence that is earned rather than borrowed. This overlay can steady you or shrink you. Ask whether their standards help you grow, and push back when they only diminish you.",
    2: "With their Saturn in your 2nd house, they bring caution and discipline to your finances and self-worth. They may help you budget, save and build long-term security in a way you could not manage alone. You could also feel that they limit your spending or undervalue what you care about. This overlay rewards patience and planning. Use their practicality to build real stability, and protect your right to enjoy what you earn.",
    3: "Their Saturn falls in your 3rd house, so communication can feel heavy or overly careful. They may correct your ideas, slow conversations down or make you weigh every word. Over time you can learn to think and speak with more precision and authority. You might also feel censored, unheard or nervous about saying the wrong thing. Keep talking regularly and honestly, and tell them plainly when their seriousness shuts you down.",
    4: "When their Saturn lands in your 4th house, home and family matters take on real weight. They may bring structure and reliability to your private life, or remind you uncomfortably of a strict parent. You might feel responsible for them, or pressured about how domestic life should run. This overlay can build a solid home over years. It can also feel cold. Make warmth a deliberate practice, and discuss family expectations openly.",
    5: "Their Saturn in your 5th house can dampen spontaneity. You may feel less playful or creative around them, as though fun needs permission or a good reason. On the other hand, they can help you take your creative work seriously or commit to a romance for the long haul. Watch for self-consciousness creeping into love and play. Deliberately make time for silliness, and ask them to join in rather than supervise.",
    6: "With their Saturn in your 6th house, they bring discipline to your routines, work and health. They may help you build solid habits, keep appointments and take responsibility for your body. You could also feel burdened, micromanaged or judged for how you spend your days. This overlay suits working relationships well. Balance duty with rest, and notice early if their expectations start to cost you your wellbeing.",
    7: "Their Saturn in your 7th house is a classic commitment overlay. The relationship tends to feel serious, lasting and full of responsibility, and they can be steady and loyal through hard times. There can also be coldness, fear of rejection or a heavy sense of obligation. This bond often deepens with age if both of you do the work. Honour the commitment, and keep warmth, humour and tenderness alive alongside it.",
    8: "When their Saturn falls in your 8th house, intimacy can feel guarded or slow to open. You may be cautious about trust, sex or merging resources with them, and they may be cautious too. They can also help you face old fears and build a deep, lasting security. This overlay rewards patience and honesty. Talk openly about what frightens you, and do not let control over money or closeness become a way of staying safe.",
    9: "Their Saturn in your 9th house tests your beliefs. They may question your worldview, bring discipline to your studies or make travel feel complicated and effortful. Through their influence you can develop a more grounded, tested philosophy that holds up under pressure. You might also feel your enthusiasm dampened or your dreams dismissed. Let them sharpen your thinking, and fiercely protect your curiosity and sense of wonder.",
    10: "With their Saturn in your 10th house, they take your career very seriously. They may mentor you, hold you to high standards or become an authority figure in your public life. That structure can help you achieve something lasting and respected. It can also feel like constant pressure or quiet judgement of your progress. Welcome the discipline they bring, and make sure the goals you are working toward are genuinely your own.",
    11: "Their Saturn lands in your 11th house, so friendships and future plans take on a more serious tone. They may help you commit to realistic goals and follow through, or you might feel they limit your social life and cool your dreams. This overlay can produce a loyal friendship that lasts for decades. Balance their practicality with your optimism, and keep your wider circle open enough that you can still breathe.",
    12: "When their Saturn falls in your 12th house, they touch your hidden fears. You may feel uneasy or tested around them in ways that are hard to explain, and old guilt or insecurity can surface without warning. This overlay can be deeply healing if you face those fears together with compassion. It can also feel like a silent weight you carry alone. Talk about what feels heavy, and find support beyond the relationship too."
  },
  uranus: {
    1: "Their Uranus in your 1st house shakes up how you see yourself. Around them you may feel freer, more experimental and ready to change your look, your habits or your whole direction. The connection can be electric and exciting, full of surprises. You might also feel unsettled, never quite sure what to expect from one week to the next. Enjoy the liberation, and anchor it with some steady habits so change does not become chaos.",
    2: "With their Uranus in your 2nd house, your finances and values may go through surprises. They may inspire unusual ways of earning, or unsettle your sense of financial security. You could find yourself questioning what you really value and why. This overlay is exciting but unpredictable, with sudden gains and sudden costs. Keep a solid safety net, and use their influence to update outdated values rather than throwing everything out.",
    3: "Their Uranus falls in your 3rd house, so conversations are stimulating and full of surprises. They introduce you to unusual ideas and new ways of thinking, and you may find yourself changing your mind about things you thought were settled. Their comments can be refreshing or jarring. Communication may be erratic, with long silences and sudden bursts. Enjoy the inventiveness, and agree on simple ways to stay reliably in touch.",
    4: "When their Uranus lands in your 4th house, home life becomes less predictable. They may encourage a move, an unusual living arrangement or a clean break from family patterns. This can free you from expectations you have outgrown. It can also disturb your sense of stability and belonging. Welcome the fresh air they bring, and protect at least one corner of your life where you can rest and feel completely safe.",
    5: "Their Uranus in your 5th house brings excitement and spontaneity to romance and creativity. Attraction can arrive suddenly, like a jolt, and fun comes in unexpected forms. You may try things you have never tried before and discover new sides of yourself. This overlay can be thrilling but unstable. Enjoy the spark, and talk honestly about whether you both want freedom, commitment or something unusual in between.",
    6: "With their Uranus in your 6th house, your routines, job or health habits may change. They could introduce new tools, schedules or ways of working, and daily life may become more interesting or simply more disrupted. This overlay can suit inventive work together, especially in technology or unconventional fields. Keep a basic structure that supports your health and sleep while you experiment with everything else.",
    7: "Their Uranus in your 7th house brings excitement and unpredictability to partnership. You may be drawn to them precisely because they are different and free. The relationship may be unconventional, long-distance or on again, off again. This overlay needs space and a lot of honesty. Build a partnership that allows real independence, and be clear with each other about what commitment actually means to each of you.",
    8: "When their Uranus falls in your 8th house, intimacy can be electric and unpredictable. They may awaken new sides of your sexuality or shake your usual ways of trusting. Shared finances could also see sudden changes. This overlay can bring real breakthroughs in how you handle vulnerability and control. Keep communication honest and frequent, and check that excitement is not quietly replacing emotional safety.",
    9: "Their Uranus in your 9th house opens your mind to new beliefs and experiences. They may inspire unusual travel, radical ideas or a break from the thinking you inherited. You can feel liberated, curious and wide awake. There can also be restlessness or sudden changes of direction that leave you dizzy. Enjoy the awakening, and ground your new perspectives in how you actually live and treat people.",
    10: "With their Uranus in your 10th house, they shake up your career and reputation. They may encourage a bold change of direction, a new path or a less conventional public image. This can free you from a role that no longer fits and was quietly draining you. It can also bring instability or professional risk. Welcome the courage they spark, and make big changes with a plan rather than on impulse.",
    11: "Their Uranus lands in your 11th house, so friendship feels exciting and forward-looking. They may introduce you to new people, causes or ideas about the future, and the bond has a free-spirited, slightly rebellious quality. It can also be unpredictable, with the friendship coming and going. Enjoy the stimulation, and accept that this connection may thrive best with plenty of room and few demands.",
    12: "When their Uranus falls in your 12th house, they awaken hidden parts of you. Sudden insights, vivid dreams or unexpected emotional releases may arise in their presence. This overlay can free you from old fears you had stopped noticing. It can also feel unsettling, as though they have disturbed something buried that you were not ready to look at. Give yourself time to process, and keep a grounding practice close."
  },
  neptune: {
    1: "Their Neptune in your 1st house can make them see you through a romantic haze. You may feel idealised, inspired or softened around them, and the connection often has a dreamy, almost magical quality. The risk is that they fall for a fantasy rather than the real you, or that you blur your edges trying to match their picture. Enjoy the enchantment, and keep gently showing them who you truly are, flaws included.",
    2: "With their Neptune in your 2nd house, money and values can become blurry. They may inspire you to value creative or spiritual things more, or encourage a new generosity in you. There can also be confusion, vagueness or even deception around finances, whether intended or not. Keep records clear and agreements explicit, and let their influence refine your values without clouding your practical decisions.",
    3: "Their Neptune falls in your 3rd house, so communication is intuitive and poetic. You may feel you understand each other without words, and conversations can be imaginative, tender and inspiring. Misunderstandings are also likely, because so much gets assumed rather than said. Plans can drift. Check in plainly about practical matters like times, places and money, and enjoy the creative, dreamy flow everywhere else.",
    4: "When their Neptune lands in your 4th house, home can feel like a sanctuary or a mystery. They may bring beauty, music or a spiritual atmosphere into your private life, and you might idealise the idea of living together. There can also be confusion or unmet expectations about family roles and household practicalities. Keep home life honest and workable, and treat the magic as a bonus rather than the foundation.",
    5: "Their Neptune in your 5th house brings romance, fantasy and creative inspiration. Love can feel like a film, and creative collaboration can be genuinely magical. You may be completely swept away. The risk is idealisation, or not seeing clearly what is being offered. Enjoy the enchantment, and keep one foot on the ground by paying attention to how they actually behave over time, not only how they make you feel.",
    6: "With their Neptune in your 6th house, daily routines and health can become either inspired or vague. They may encourage gentler rhythms, creative work or healing practices like yoga and meditation. You might also find your routines slipping, deadlines blurring or your energy draining without a clear cause. Keep practical structures in place, and notice honestly whether their influence nourishes your wellbeing or muddies it.",
    7: "Their Neptune in your 7th house brings idealism to partnership. You may see them as a soulmate, or as someone you need to rescue or be rescued by. The connection can be deeply compassionate and spiritual. It can also involve illusions, disappointment or blurred boundaries about who is responsible for what. Love with open eyes, and keep checking that you are relating to a real person, not only to a dream.",
    8: "When their Neptune falls in your 8th house, intimacy can feel transcendent. Sex and emotional closeness may carry a spiritual, merging quality that is hard to find elsewhere. There can also be confusion around shared money or trust, or a tendency to lose yourself entirely in the bond. Keep finances transparent and conversations honest, and make sure deep connection never requires you to dissolve your boundaries.",
    9: "Their Neptune in your 9th house inspires your spiritual life and imagination. They may introduce you to mysticism, art, music or dreamlike travel, and you can feel uplifted and more open to meaning. There is also a risk of idealising a belief system, a teacher or each other, and of being misled as a result. Explore freely and with an open heart, and keep your discernment switched firmly on.",
    10: "With their Neptune in your 10th house, they may inspire your career, especially in creative, healing or caring fields. They can help you imagine a more meaningful public life. They could also cloud your professional judgement, or project a glamorous image onto your work that does not match reality. Enjoy the vision they bring, and stay practical about goals, contracts and the reputation you are actually building.",
    11: "Their Neptune lands in your 11th house, so friendship has an idealistic, compassionate quality. You may share dreams, causes or spiritual interests, and the bond can feel quietly meaningful. There can also be vagueness about plans, unreliable follow-through or disappointments within group settings. Enjoy the shared vision and the gentleness between you, and turn at least some of the dreaming into concrete steps.",
    12: "When their Neptune falls in your 12th house, the connection feels deeply spiritual and hard to put into words. You may feel you have known them before, or that they reach your soul in a way few people do. This can be profoundly healing and inspiring. It can also bring confusion, escapism or secrecy. Stay grounded in daily life, and let the depth lead you toward clarity rather than away from it."
  },
  pluto: {
    1: "Their Pluto in your 1st house makes them powerfully aware of you, and you of them. You may feel scrutinised, magnetised or quietly remade in their presence, as though they see beneath every mask you wear. This can push you to become more authentic and resilient than you have ever been. It can also slide into control over how you look or act. Let the intensity strengthen you, and never hand them the right to define you.",
    2: "With their Pluto in your 2nd house, they can transform your relationship with money, possessions and self-worth. They may help you build real financial power, or expose insecurities you did not know you carried. Old attachments to things or status can fall away. There is also potential for control over resources, or struggles over who earns and owns what. Keep your own income and choices intact while you grow.",
    3: "Their Pluto falls in your 3rd house, so conversations go straight to the bone. They may probe your thinking, uncover what you really believe and change the way you speak and write. Talking with them can feel penetrating, even obsessive at times. This overlay can deepen your mind remarkably. It can also bring manipulation or cutting words. Keep communication honest and direct, and walk away from conversations that turn into interrogation.",
    4: "When their Pluto lands in your 4th house, they reach into your roots. They may stir up family history, old wounds or deep questions about where you belong. Living together can be intense and life-changing. This overlay can clear out old family patterns for good, but it can also feel like your private sanctuary has been invaded. Protect your need for safety, and let the transformation happen at a pace you can sustain.",
    5: "Their Pluto in your 5th house makes romance and creativity intense. Attraction can be obsessive, and the relationship may feel like a grand passion that consumes everything else. They can push your creative self-expression to real depth and courage. There is also a risk of jealousy, control or drama in love. Enjoy the fire, and keep your self-respect, your friendships and your sense of play firmly your own.",
    6: "With their Pluto in your 6th house, they can overhaul your daily routines, work habits and health. They may push you to fix what is broken, from diet to workplace dynamics, and the changes can be dramatic. Working together can be deeply productive or quietly controlling. Welcome the push to improve, and watch for anyone trying to manage your body, schedule or job more than is fair or healthy.",
    7: "Their Pluto in your 7th house makes partnership a transformative force in your life. The bond can feel fated and all-encompassing, and it often changes both of you for good. It can also bring power struggles, possessiveness or a battle over who leads. This overlay asks for radical honesty and equal footing. Face the intensity directly, keep your own sources of strength, and never trade your freedom for closeness.",
    8: "When their Pluto falls in your 8th house, the connection runs very deep. Intimacy, sex and shared resources carry enormous power, and the relationship may reshape how you trust, desire and let go. You may feel utterly bound to them. This overlay can be profoundly healing and transformative. It can also turn controlling or obsessive. Keep consent, honesty and clear financial boundaries at the centre, and trust what your body tells you.",
    9: "Their Pluto in your 9th house challenges your beliefs to their core. They may shatter old worldviews, draw you into intense study or send you on journeys that change your perspective permanently. You can emerge with a deeper, hard-won philosophy. There can also be ideological battles or a pull toward extremes. Let them deepen your understanding, and keep your right to believe what rings true for you.",
    10: "With their Pluto in your 10th house, they have a powerful effect on your career and public life. They may push you toward real influence and success, or bring upheaval to your reputation and professional path. You might feel driven, even compelled, to achieve more. This overlay can also bring control over your ambitions. Harness the power they stir up, and make sure your choices reflect your own values, not theirs.",
    11: "Their Pluto lands in your 11th house, so they transform your friendships and hopes for the future. They may bring you into powerful groups, shake up your social circle or change what you want from life. Some old friendships may fall away. This overlay can be deeply empowering, or intense and controlling within shared networks. Stay true to your own goals, and choose your allies with care rather than by pull.",
    12: "When their Pluto falls in your 12th house, they touch the deepest layers of your unconscious. Old fears, secrets or buried grief may surface around them, sometimes without either of you understanding why. This can lead to profound healing and release. It can also feel frightening or disorienting, as though they hold power you cannot see. Get support for what arises, and bring hidden dynamics into the open gently and steadily."
  },
  northNode: {
    1: "Their North Node in your 1st house suggests they help you grow into who you are becoming. Around them you may feel called to be more independent, visible and self-directed than you have been. There is often a sense of purpose in the connection, as though it is nudging you forward. It can feel uncomfortable at times, because growth rarely feels easy. Welcome the push toward self-definition, and let it be your own.",
    2: "With their North Node in your 2nd house, the relationship encourages you to build steadier values and resources. They may prompt you to take your talents, income and self-worth more seriously, and to invest in what genuinely matters to you. The connection can feel purposeful and grounding. It may also bring you face to face with old insecurities about money or worth. Treat it as a chance to grow sturdier roots.",
    3: "Their North Node falls in your 3rd house, so this connection supports growth through learning, talking and staying curious. They may encourage you to write, study, speak up or reconnect with siblings and neighbours. Conversations feel meaningful, as though they carry something you need to hear. It can stretch you out of fixed opinions. Stay open to their questions, and let everyday exchanges become part of your development.",
    4: "When their North Node lands in your 4th house, the relationship points you toward home, family and emotional roots. They may help you build a home, reconnect with family or explore your inner life more fully than you have before. There can be a sense of coming home to yourself. It may also pull you away from outer ambitions for a while. Trust that tending your foundations is real growth.",
    5: "Their North Node in your 5th house invites you to open up to joy, love and creative expression. They may encourage you to play, create, take romantic risks or explore parenting. There is a sense that the relationship helps you rediscover delight. It can feel exposing if you are used to holding back. Let yourself shine, have fun and take pleasure seriously as part of your path.",
    6: "With their North Node in your 6th house, the connection encourages healthier routines and meaningful work. They may inspire you to look after your body, become more organised or find a job that truly suits you. There is a sense of purpose in the ordinary details. It can feel demanding when you would rather escape into dreams. Commit to practical improvements, and trust that daily habits shape your growth.",
    7: "Their North Node in your 7th house often points to a significant partnership. The relationship helps you learn about cooperation, compromise and committed love, and you may sense it is meant to teach you something important. It can also challenge an old habit of doing everything alone. Welcome the chance to share your life more fully, while still keeping a clear sense of who you are.",
    8: "When their North Node falls in your 8th house, the connection pulls you toward depth and transformation. They may encourage deeper intimacy, emotional honesty or a new relationship with shared money and power. There is often a sense of necessary change. It can feel frightening to let go of control or comfort. Trust that vulnerability is part of the growth, and move at a pace you can actually manage.",
    9: "Their North Node in your 9th house inspires you to expand your horizons. They may encourage travel, further study, spiritual exploration or a new philosophy of life. There is a sense that the connection is broadening you in lasting ways. It can challenge a habit of staying small or overthinking details. Follow the invitation toward meaning, and let adventure become part of your path.",
    10: "With their North Node in your 10th house, they point you toward your purpose in the world. They may encourage your career ambitions, help you step into leadership or push you toward public recognition. The relationship can feel like a catalyst for your life's work. It may also pull you out of your comfort zone at home. Take the opportunity seriously, and define success in a way that fits you.",
    11: "Their North Node lands in your 11th house, so the connection guides you toward community and future goals. They may introduce you to groups, causes or friends who matter to your growth. There is a sense of shared vision and collective purpose. It can challenge a tendency to seek only personal recognition. Invest in friendships and long-term dreams, and let the relationship widen your circle.",
    12: "When their North Node falls in your 12th house, the relationship draws you toward spiritual growth and inner healing. They may encourage meditation, retreat, therapy or quiet reflection. There is often a sense of being called to let go of control and trust something larger. This can feel disorienting if you are used to structure and certainty. Honour the invitation to rest, reflect and heal."
  },
  chiron: {
    1: "Their Chiron in your 1st house touches your sense of self. They may unintentionally poke at insecurities about your appearance, identity or confidence, and you might feel oddly exposed around them. They can also help you heal those wounds by seeing you with compassion. This overlay invites honest conversations about sensitivity. Tell them what hurts, and let the connection help you accept yourself more fully.",
    2: "With their Chiron in your 2nd house, they may stir up old wounds around money, security or self-worth. You might feel inadequate or undervalued at times, even if they do not mean it that way. They can also help you rebuild your sense of worth and find value in your talents. This overlay asks for gentleness about resources. Name your insecurities, and let healing replace comparison.",
    3: "Their Chiron falls in your 3rd house, so communication can touch old wounds. You may feel misunderstood, criticised or hesitant to speak up around them, perhaps echoing earlier experiences at school or with siblings. They can also help you find your voice and heal those memories. Speak slowly and kindly to each other, and let honest conversation become a place of repair.",
    4: "When their Chiron lands in your 4th house, family wounds may surface. They might remind you of childhood hurts or unresolved issues with parents, and home can feel tender. The connection can also help you heal your roots and create a safer emotional base. This overlay asks for patience and compassion. Share your history with care, and build new patterns of safety together.",
    5: "Their Chiron in your 5th house touches your joy, creativity and romance. You may feel self-conscious about expressing yourself, having fun or being loved, and old hurts about play or recognition may resurface. They can also help you reclaim your delight and creative confidence. Be gentle with your inner child, and let the relationship become a safe space for play.",
    6: "With their Chiron in your 6th house, they may bring attention to health, work or daily routines that need healing. You might feel sensitive about your body, habits or job performance around them, as though they notice every slip. They can also help you create kinder routines and a more compassionate approach to wellbeing. Treat vulnerabilities as information, not failures, and build supportive habits together.",
    7: "Their Chiron in your 7th house touches old wounds around partnership. You may feel afraid of rejection, betrayal or imbalance, even when they mean well. The relationship can also become a place where those wounds heal through patience and honesty. This overlay asks for gentle communication and mutual respect. Face the tender spots together, and build trust slowly and deliberately.",
    8: "When their Chiron falls in your 8th house, intimacy can feel tender and raw. Old wounds around trust, sexuality or loss may surface in their presence. This overlay can be profoundly healing if both of you approach vulnerability with care. It can also stir fear or defensiveness. Take your time with closeness, talk about boundaries openly and let healing happen gradually.",
    9: "Their Chiron in your 9th house touches your beliefs and sense of meaning. You may feel insecure about your education, faith or worldview around them, or find old disappointments resurfacing. They can also help you discover a more compassionate philosophy, one that makes room for doubt and for not knowing. Let the connection become a place to question safely, and trust that wisdom often grows from wounds.",
    10: "With their Chiron in your 10th house, they touch wounds around career, recognition or public image. You may feel inadequate about your achievements, compare yourself with them or fear being judged for where you have landed so far. They can also help you heal those fears and find a more authentic sense of purpose. Share your ambitions honestly, and let their encouragement soften your inner critic.",
    11: "Their Chiron lands in your 11th house, so friendship and belonging may feel tender. You might feel like an outsider around them or their friends, or old hurts from groups may surface. They can also help you heal those wounds and find where you truly belong. Be patient with social discomfort, and let the connection show you what healthy friendship looks like.",
    12: "When their Chiron falls in your 12th house, they touch deep, hidden wounds. You may feel an unexplained sadness, fear or vulnerability around them, as though something old is surfacing. This can be a powerful healing connection if you both approach it with compassion. Get support where needed, and trust that bringing hidden pain into the light is part of letting it go."
  }
};
